<!--
  Malachi's mark: a solid shield with a bar cut clean through it.

  One shape and one hole, and that is the whole point. What was here before drew a shield in
  4.5px strokes with a prohibition sign inside it — two ideas competing in a space that ends up
  48dp on a real launcher, where those strokes are barely more than a hair and the ring inside
  them is a smudge. A filled silhouette carries at any size; the bar is negative space rather
  than a third colour, so the background's teal shows through it and the icon stays two tones.

  A bar and not a diagonal slash on purpose: a line drawn across a shield reads as a shield
  crossed out — the protection disabled, which is the opposite of what this app does. A bar
  through it reads the way it does on a road sign: nothing gets past.

  Everything is inside the 66dp circle that an adaptive icon guarantees is visible, so no
  launcher mask can clip a corner of it: the widest points sit ~31dp from the centre of the
  108dp canvas, against the 33dp the safe zone allows.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
